what = IntroWhat(
  "A battle-tested 2D rendering library that provides a hierarchical scene graph, automatic draw-call batching, multi-texture optimization, custom filters, and asset management for 60+ FPS web graphics.",
  "PixiJS is a rendering engine that allows you to create rich, interactive 2D graphics, cross-platform applications, and games using WebGL and WebGPU without dealing with complex lower-level shader code.",
  [
    "Hierarchical Scene Graph: Tree structure with Containers, Sprites, Graphics, and Text",
    "Automatic Batch Rendering: Bundles thousands of draw calls into single GPU passes",
    "WebGL & WebGPU Dual Backends: Modern hardware acceleration with automatic fallbacks",
    "Asset Management & Texture Atlases: Asynchronous loading, caching, and sprite sheet slicing",
  ],
  ["PixiJS", "WebGL", "WebGPU", "2D Graphics", "Game Engine"],
)

why = IntroWhy(
  "Raw HTML5 2D Canvas struggles when animating thousands of objects due to CPU rasterization bottlenecks, while raw WebGL requires hundreds of lines of shader setup and matrix math boilerplate.",
  "PixiJS bridges this gap by offering a clean, intuitive display tree API while unlocking the full speed of the GPU, powering interactive maps, data visualizations, and production web games at locked 60 FPS.",
)
